# Line-ending contract (D-13). Decided deliberately at the head of the v2 restructure,
# while a whole-tree renormalisation is still cheap.
#
# Every pre-existing blob in this repository stored CRLF (main.js: 632 CRLF, 0 bare LF)
# because core.autocrlf=true was active with no .gitattributes. Left alone, the first .ts
# file added by plan 01-02 would be stored LF while every existing blob was CRLF - a latent
# whole-tree diff that would surface later as "whole file changed" on a file nobody edited.
# text=auto normalises blobs to LF; eol=crlf checks them out as CRLF, which is what a
# Windows-first project wants. Applied in one isolated commit so it reverts as a unit.

* text=auto eol=crlf

# Binary: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.db  binary

# POSIX tools read these byte-for-byte. A shell script checked out with CRLF hands bash a
# shebang ending in a carriage return; it fails as "bad interpreter", which reads like a
# missing binary rather than a line-ending bug. Ubuntu CI runs tools/baseline/*.sh (plan 01-04).
*.sh   text eol=lf
.nvmrc text eol=lf

# CUSTODY-09 baseline artifacts are written by tools/baseline/inventory.sh, a POSIX shell
# script, and are re-generated and diffed in Phase 8 to prove behaviour parity. Under the
# tree-wide `eol=crlf` rule they check out CRLF while the generator writes LF, which leaves
# `git status` permanently reporting them as modified even though `git diff` is empty - the
# exact "noise" the determinism requirement exists to avoid. Pin them to LF so the checked-out
# bytes and the generated bytes are the same on Windows and on the Ubuntu CI runner.
baselines/** text eol=lf

# Same reasoning as baselines/** above, for the generated SQL fixtures (plan 01-04, extended
# by plan 01-07). tests/fixtures/*.sql is written by tools/baseline/archive-real-db.mjs and by
# the fixture generator, both of which emit LF. Under the tree-wide `eol=crlf` rule the file
# checks out CRLF, so every regeneration leaves `git status` reporting a byte-identical file as
# modified - noise around the one artifact whose regeneration must be unambiguous (D-05: plan
# 01-07 diffs this extract against its own fixture to decide whether a second legacy variant
# exists). Pin to LF so the checked-out bytes and the generated bytes match on Windows and on
# the Ubuntu CI runner alike.
tests/fixtures/*.sql text eol=lf

# Vendored capture assets (plan 01-05). These are not source: they are byte-exact copies of what
# cdn.tailwindcss.com and fonts.googleapis.com served on a particular day, and their SHA-256 is
# recorded in baselines/v1.2.1/MANIFEST.md so that a Phase 8 re-capture is diffed against a fixed
# target rather than a moving one. Under the tree-wide `eol=crlf` rule, tailwind.js and the two
# stylesheets would be fetched as LF, stored as LF and CHECKED OUT AS CRLF - so every digest in the
# manifest would fail to verify on a fresh clone, for a file nobody had touched.
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion in both directions while leaving the files diffable.
tools/baseline/vendor/** -text

# Fonts are binary. `text=auto` would very probably detect that on its own; saying so explicitly
# costs one line and removes the "very probably" from an artifact whose corruption would be
# invisible until a baseline render came out wrong.
*.woff2 binary
